# netsurf: Vita frontend runs pages' JavaScript through the QuickJS bridge (frontends/vita)
# Generated 2026-09-23
#
# QuickJS step 2, the frontend half (core: patch 44; backend: patch 45).
# - Makefile.defaults: NETSURF_USE_QUICKJS=YES (Duktape stays off).
# - js_platform.c/.h (new): the services quickjs/macos9.h declares --
#   macos9_schedule / _cancel_owner / sched_is_queued on the Vita scheduler,
#   allocation, TickCount, performance.now()'s clock, crypto random bytes
#   from getentropy() (sceKernelGetRandomNumber on the Vita), the text
#   measurement table, the JS-time profile counter.
# - schedule.c/.h: remove every callback of an owner (a destroyed content
#   takes its pending callbacks with it) and an is-queued query.
# - main.c: enable_javascript on; the bridge's event loop
#   (macsurf_qjs_pump_all: timers, promise jobs, queued events) every pass
#   of the main loop, as MacSurf's main loop runs it; a page is not
#   "settled" while a script-driven relayout is pending for it; the
#   JS-dom and JS-fetch test pages.
# - diag.c: macsurf_debug_log_write (MS_LOG, so also the page's
#   console.log) into netsurf.log; the compat fallback wrote to stderr.
# - qjs_hooks.c: the engine counters are the bridge's when it is linked.
# See docs/phase-0/10-hardware-test-plan.md §Run 10.

